---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
import Formula from '../../../components/Formula.astro';

const f = {
  fwd: "$$\\text{cups} = \\text{fl oz} \\div 8$$",
  rev: "$$\\text{fl oz} = \\text{cups} \\times 8$$",
};

const tocItems = [
  { id: 'how-to-use',      label: 'How to use this converter' },
  { id: 'formula',         label: 'How to convert fl oz to cups' },
  { id: 'reference-table', label: 'fl oz to cups reference table' },
  { id: 'faq',             label: 'FAQs' },
  { id: 'related-tools',   label: 'Related tools' },
];

const schema = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "WebApplication",
    "name": "Fluid Ounces to Cups Converter",
    "url": "https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/fl-oz-to-cup",
    "description": "Convert US fluid ounces to cups. 8 fl oz = 1 cup, 4 fl oz = 0.5 cups, 12 fl oz = 1.5 cups. All US measurements.",
    "applicationCategory": "UtilitiesApplication",
    "operatingSystem": "Any",
    "browserRequirements": "Requires JavaScript",
    "isAccessibleForFree": true,
    "offers": { "@type": "Offer", "price": "0", "priceCurrency": "USD" }
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "HowTo",
    "name": "How to convert fluid ounces to cups",
    "description": "Divide fluid ounces by 8 to get US cups.",
    "step": [
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 1, "name": "Enter fl oz value", "text": "Type your fl oz value in the fl oz field. The cup result updates instantly." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 2, "name": "Read the result", "text": "The converted cup value appears. For 8 fl oz, the result is 1 cup." },
      { "@type": "HowToStep", "position": 3, "name": "Convert in reverse", "text": "Type in the cups field to convert back to fl oz." }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "mainEntity": [
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many cups is 8 fl oz?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "8 fl oz equals exactly 1 cup. The US cup is defined as 8 fl oz, so this is a whole-number conversion." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many cups is 12 fl oz?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "12 fl oz equals 1.5 cups. Divide 12 by 8: 12 ÷ 8 = 1.5 cups. A standard US 12 fl oz can is 1.5 cups." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many cups is 16 fl oz?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "16 fl oz equals 2 cups. Divide 16 by 8: 16 ÷ 8 = 2 cups. This is also 1 US pint." } },
      { "@type": "Question", "name": "How many cups is 32 fl oz?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "32 fl oz equals 4 cups. Divide 32 by 8: 32 ÷ 8 = 4 cups. This is 1 US quart." } }
    ]
  }
];
---
<CalculatorLayout
  title="Fluid Ounces to Cups Converter"
  metaTitle="Fluid Ounces to Cups Converter | Convert fl oz to cups"
  description="Convert fl oz to US cups. 8 fl oz = 1 cup, 12 fl oz = 1.5 cups, 16 fl oz = 2 cups = 1 pint, 32 fl oz = 4 cups = 1 quart. Enter fl oz or cups."
  canonical="https://calculations.tools/conversion/volume-converter/fl-oz-to-cup"
  tocItems={tocItems}
  embedSlug="fl-oz-to-cup"
  schema={schema}
  ogFormula="cups = fl oz ÷ 8"
  ogExample="8 fl oz = 1 cup"
>
  <div slot="calculator">
    <section class="calculator-interface">
      <div class="calculator-container">
        <div class="calculator-header">
          <h2>Instantly Convert fl oz to cups</h2>
          <p>Type in either field - converts instantly in both directions</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-inputs">
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-a">Fluid Ounces (fl oz)</label>
            <input id="lp-a" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 8" />
          </div>
          <div class="pair-eq">=</div>
          <div class="pair-field">
            <label for="lp-b">Cups</label>
            <input id="lp-b" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 1" />
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pair-formula-note">1 cup = 8 fl oz &nbsp;·&nbsp; US measurements</div>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script src="/js/fl-oz-to-cup.js" is:inline></script>
  </div>
  <div slot="content">
    <div class="seo-container">
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Quick answer</div>
        <p>To convert fluid ounces to cups, divide by <strong>8</strong>. So 8 fl oz = 1 cup, 4 fl oz = 0.5 cups, and 16 fl oz = 2 cups (1 pint). This is exact: 1 US cup = 8 US fl oz by definition.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="answer-box">
        <div class="answer-box-label">Key takeaways</div>
        <ul>
          <li>Exact formula: cups = fl oz ÷ 8. 1 cup = 8 fl oz exactly.</li>
          <li>4 fl oz = 1/2 cup. 8 fl oz = 1 cup. 12 fl oz = 1.5 cups. 16 fl oz = 2 cups (1 pint).</li>
          <li>Quick check: a standard US 12 oz can is 1.5 cups. A 32 oz bottle is 4 cups (1 quart).</li>
          <li>Reverse: fl oz = cups × 8.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <h2 id="how-to-use">How to use our fl oz to cups converter</h2>
      <p>Type any fl oz value in the fl oz field and the cup result appears instantly. Both directions work without pressing a button.</p>
      <h2 id="formula">How do you convert fl oz to cups?</h2>
      <p>Divide the number of fluid ounces by 8. The US cup is defined as 8 fl oz, so this is an exact whole-number conversion for even fl oz values, and a simple decimal for odd values.</p>
      <Formula expr={f.fwd} />
      <p>Worked examples: 2 fl oz = 0.25 cups (1/4). 4 fl oz = 0.5 cups (1/2). 6 fl oz = 0.75 cups (3/4). 8 fl oz = 1 cup. 12 fl oz = 1.5 cups. 16 fl oz = 2 cups. 32 fl oz = 4 cups.</p>
      <h2 id="reference-table">Fluid ounces to cups reference table</h2>
      <p>Standard fl oz values converted to cups, with cup fraction and volume context:</p>
      <div class="responsive-table">
        <table>
          <thead>
            <tr><th>Fluid Ounces</th><th>Cups</th><th>Context</th></tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>1 fl oz</td><td>0.125 (1/8)</td><td>2 tablespoons</td></tr>
            <tr><td>2 fl oz</td><td>0.25 (1/4)</td><td>4 tablespoons</td></tr>
            <tr><td>4 fl oz</td><td>0.5 (1/2)</td><td>Half cup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>6 fl oz</td><td>0.75 (3/4)</td><td>Three-quarter cup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>8 fl oz</td><td>1 cup</td><td>Standard cup</td></tr>
            <tr><td>10 fl oz</td><td>1.25 cups</td><td>Large glass</td></tr>
            <tr><td>12 fl oz</td><td>1.5 cups</td><td>Standard US can</td></tr>
            <tr><td>16 fl oz</td><td>2 cups</td><td>1 pint</td></tr>
            <tr><td>24 fl oz</td><td>3 cups</td><td>Large water bottle</td></tr>
            <tr><td>32 fl oz</td><td>4 cups</td><td>1 quart</td></tr>
            <tr><td>64 fl oz</td><td>8 cups</td><td>Half gallon</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2 id="faq">FAQs about fl oz to cups conversion</h2>
      <h3>How many cups is 8 fl oz?</h3>
      <p>8 fl oz equals exactly 1 cup. 8 ÷ 8 = 1. The cup is defined as 8 fl oz in the US customary system.</p>
      <h3>How many cups is 12 fl oz?</h3>
      <p>12 fl oz equals 1.5 cups. 12 ÷ 8 = 1.5 cups. A standard 12 fl oz US can holds 1.5 cups of liquid.</p>
      <h3>How many cups is 16 fl oz?</h3>
      <p>16 fl oz equals 2 cups. 16 ÷ 8 = 2 cups. 16 fl oz is also 1 US pint.</p>
      <h3>How many cups is 32 fl oz?</h3>
      <p>32 fl oz equals 4 cups. 32 ÷ 8 = 4 cups. 32 fl oz is also 1 US quart or 2 pints.</p>
      <h2 id="related-tools">Related tools</h2>
      <ul class="related-tools-list">
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/cup-to-fl-oz">Cups to Fluid Ounces</a>
            <p>Reverse conversion - enter cups and get fl oz instantly.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/fl-oz-to-ml">Fluid Ounces to Milliliters</a>
            <p>Convert fl oz to ml - 8 fl oz = 236.6 ml.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter/cup-to-ml">Cups to Milliliters</a>
            <p>Convert cups to ml - 1 cup = 236.6 ml.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="tool-icon">💧</span>
          <div>
            <a href="/conversion/volume-converter">Volume Converter (all units)</a>
            <p>Convert between all volume units - ml, L, fl oz, cups, gallons, and more.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</CalculatorLayout>
<style is:global>
  .pair-inputs { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 0.75rem; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .pair-field label { display: block; font-size: 0.8rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-field input { width: 100%; padding: 0.6rem 0.75rem; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.08); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.15); border-radius: 8px; color: white; font-size: 1rem; box-sizing: border-box; }
  .pair-eq { font-size: 1.5rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.5); padding-bottom: 0.35rem; }
  .pair-formula-note { text-align: center; font-size: 0.75rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.45); margin-top: 0.5rem; }
  @media (max-width: 480px) { .pair-inputs { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .pair-eq { text-align: center; padding-bottom: 0; } }
</style>